 "notes": "E6 test case dataset. Two state tenants of 500 field workers, eight NGO tenants sharing 500, at day 180. Only encounter volume differs between the three; beneficiary population does not grow with programme activity. bundle_path and bundle_revision must be filled in before generating. A tenant may also carry its own bundle_path, which is how H1's 'cover the range of organisation size' is done -- config size drives the syncDetails row count -- without them this recipe cannot be reproduced. organisation_id is null on every tenant and must be filled in before generating. It held 1-10, which are not free: on the load environment 1 is the platform organisation, 3 the customer's, 9 a fixture and 10 the first state tenant. Those ids were placeholders from before any tenant was provisioned, and generating against them would have written a pilot dataset into four live organisations. Provision the ten tenants, dump refs.json, and record the ids the server assigned.",
